  "two_waves_exact": "the core SMM armor (FlashSmiSmm, FlashSmiDxe, PrepareWhiteListSmm, SbRomArmorSmm + one freeform) first measures 5/7 at 3802 (2022-05-12) — the release IMMEDIATELY following 3604 (2022-03-16, 0/7) in the ledger, so the introduction is bounded to a single release gap; the set completes at 4604 (2024-04-08) when the DXE helper 4EB43107 and the second freeform join; 3810-4402 all sit at 5/7",
  "ring16_reading_corrected": "ring 16 read the armor as bracketing the LogoFail year because its bisect skipped 3802/3810/4003 — with those measured, the core wave PREDATES the LogoFail disclosure (2023) by about fourteen months and cannot be a reaction to it; what DOES land inside the disclosure window is the legacy-SMM RETIREMENT: both legacy modules still present at 4003 (2023-03-21), one gone by 4202 (2023-08-02), both gone by 4402 (2024-01-08)",
  "sampling_bias_lesson": "a binary search answers only the question asked ('by when present'), never 'when introduced' — the ring-16 'present by 4202' was true and misleading at once; the ring-18 fix is three more probes, not a new theory",
  "day0_use": "checklist against the dump: 5/7 armor GUIDs expected if >= 3802 (2022-05), 7/7 if >= 4604 (2024-04); legacy pair 2/2 if <= 4003, 1/2 at 4202, 0/2 from 4402 — 0/7 overall would date the build pre-3802 and is itself a finding; read with the AGESA timeline (vendor-agesa.json) for a second independent bound"
 },
